    {
      "v": 3,
      "zh": "大 衛 王 來 到 耶 路 撒 冷 ， 進 了 宮 殿 ， 就 把 從 前 留 下 看 守 宮 殿 的 十 個 妃 嬪 禁 閉 在 冷 宮 ， 養 活 他 們 ， 不 與 他 們 親 近 。 他 們 如 同 寡 婦 被 禁 ， 直 到 死 的 日 子 。",
      "en": "Then David went to his palace[NOTE:1] in Jerusalem. The king took the 10 concubines he had left to care for the palace and placed them under confinement.[NOTE:2] Though he provided for their needs, he did not sleep with them.[NOTE:3] They remained under restriction until the day they died, living out the rest of their lives as widows.",
      "notes": [
